                <pb facs="0859" n="745" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg745"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1277: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Trueblood</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-07-06T21:00:00-04:32">July 6, 1931—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>73. The Paraguayan Minister in Bolivia has received instructions that his mission
                    has been terminated and that he is to proceed to Arica. He will depart on
                    Thursday, July 9, and will probably go to Lima where I understand he is to be
                    the Minister. He is trying to induce his Government to rescind the instructions
                    terminating his mission to Bolivia, thereby permitting him to remain nominally
                    accredited to Bolivia while serving in Peru.</p>
                <p>I understand that four military airplanes have already departed for the Chaco and
                    that within a few days others will follow. It is reported that three regiments
                    have been mobilized. In order to avoid seizure of new trucks to be used for
                    mobilization of troops in Potosí the General Motors agent at that place had to
                    complain to the Ministry of War through American representative here. The agent
                    was advised that the orders of the Ministry of War were to requisition only used
                    trucks and to pay for any use made of them.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Trueblood</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
